PlayerBot slash commands
========================

All PlayerBot commands require the PROGRAMMER role and are handled by the
normal SlashService/CommandDispatcher path. They operate on persistent bot
characters; they do not create simulated market or combat results.

  /bot status
      Show online bots and their persisted brain states.
  /bot spawn <profession> <count>
      Activate existing records for miner, hauler, mission_runner,
      rat_hunter, trader, or industrialist (up to playerbots.maxBots).
  /bot dismiss <characterID>
      Log out one bot without deleting its character, wallet, ship, or items.
  /bot follow | come | stay | dock | mine
      Issue the corresponding real movement/operation order to online bots.
  /bot order <botID|all> <follow|stay|dock|mine|attack> [targetID]
      Send a command to one online bot by characterID or to all bots. Mining
      accepts an optional asteroid typeID; attack requires a visible entityID.
  /bot attack <entityID>
      Lock and engage an entity already on the bot grid using fitted modules.
      An optional botID limits the order to one bot.
  /bot fleet
      Create/use the caller's normal fleet and invite online bots.
  /bot corp invite [corporationID] [botID]
      Move a bot into a player corporation through the normal Character corp
      membership path. With no IDs, the caller's corporation and first bot are
      used.
  /bot give <typeID> <quantity> [botID]
      Create an item through ItemFactory and place it in the bot's real cargo
      or station hangar. This is intended for controlled administration.
  /bot contract <botID> [assigneeID] [reward]
      Create a persistent courier contract row from a docked bot; reward ISK
      is escrowed from that bot's wallet and refunded if insertion fails.

Normal chat uses the configurable <playerbots><chatPrefix> (default `!`):
`!follow`, `!stay`, `!dock`, `!mine`, `!attack <entityID>`, `!fleet`, and
`!status`. Mentioning a bot by name in local, corporation, fleet, or private
chat produces a deterministic acknowledgement when optional LLM chatter is
disabled.
